  "verbalization": "The compound [(1S,2S,3R,4S,7R,9S,10S,12R,15S)-4-acetyloxy-1,9,12,15-tetrahydroxy-10,14,17,17-tetramethyl-11-oxo-6-oxatetracyclo[11.3.1.03,10.04,7]heptadec-13-en-2-yl] 3-methylbut-2-enoate] is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that this compound targets Zinc finger protein GLI1, which is a known target of Xanthotoxol, and Xanthotoxol itself has a direct interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, the compound is also shown to target another protein, 4H-1-Benzopyran-4-one, which in turn interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through the regulation of GLI1, potentially influencing epigenetic processes. The evidence is consistent with a role in the regulation of gene expression via the EZH2 complex, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
